> How are queries classified as one of the three options?
**assistant**:
> They are **not hard-classified**. The proposed implementation treats the three options as candidate `PlanSpec`s and selects the plan with the highest sampled/expected utility.
> 
> For each query:
> 
> 1. `query_features(messages)` extracts local signals, e.g.:
>    - `freshness`: “latest”, “today”, “current”
>    - `grounding_requested`: “sources”, “cite”, “evidence”
>    - `has_year`
>    - `long_query`
>    - selected cue words such as `policy`, `guidance`, `price`
> 
> 2. All eligible plans are scored:
>    - base quality prior;
>    - historical satisfaction/reliability;
>    - estimated cost and latency;
>    - learned feature-plan compatibility.
> 
> 3. `ThreeWaySelector` adds learned evidence for each active feature:
>    \[
>    P(\text{positive feedback}\mid \text{plan}, f)
>    = \frac{\alpha_{\text{plan},f}}{\alpha_{\text{plan},f}+\beta_{\text{plan},f}}
>    \]
>    A positive vote increments $\alpha$; a negative vote increments $\beta$.
> 
> 4. The selector chooses probabilistically among plans using softmax, so it can explore rather than permanently lock in early guesses.
> 
> However, the code as written has an important limitation: **at cold start, features do not prefer any option**, because every feature has a Beta(1,1) prior, i.e. 0.5. Selection initially comes mostly from plan priors, cost, and latency—likely favoring `direct_with_plan`.
> 
> I recommend adding initial cue-based adjustments, before learned evidence:
> 
> ```python
> def _cue_bonus(plan: PlanSpec, features: set[str]) -> float:
>     mode = plan.metadata.get("execution_mode")
> 
>     if mode == "direct":
>         bonus = 0.15
>         if {"freshness", "grounding_requested"} & features:
>             bonus -= 0.35
>         return bonus
> 
>     if mode == "rag":
>         bonus = 0.0
>         if "grounding_requested" in features:
>             bonus += 0.45
>         if "freshness" in features:
>             bonus += 0.35
>         if "has_year" in features:
>             bonus += 0.10
>         return bonus
> 
>     if mode == "parallel":
>         # Best where research seems likely but not certain.
>         return 0.20 if (
>             "freshness" in features or "grounding_requested" in features
>         ) else -0.15
> 
>     return 0.0
> ```
> 
> Then in `ThreeWaySelector.score_plan`:
